{
  "id": "triangular-test",
  "term": "triangular test",
  "definition": "A triangular test is a sequential boundaries method used in clinical trials to evaluate results at interim stages rather than only at the end. It is used because it can reduce the expected number of participants while preserving planned statistical standards, which gives it ethical and practical advantages in trial monitoring.",
